# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# Without these rules, what lands in a commit depends on each contributor's
# personal `core.autocrlf` setting. Git for Windows and GitHub Desktop both
# default to `true`, which writes CRLF into the working tree. That is invisible
# on Windows -- and it is how `setup_check.sh` ends up with CRLF and then fails
# the moment a student runs it in WSL or Git Bash:
#
#     setup_check.sh: line 8: $'\r': command not found
#     setup_check.sh: line 9: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#     setup_check.sh: line 24: syntax error near unexpected token `$'do\r''
#
# `text=auto` normalises everything to LF *in the repository*, while still
# letting Git write native endings into each platform's working tree. The
# `eol=lf` rules below override that for files parsed by tools that are not
# Windows tools, regardless of which platform checked them out.

* text=auto

# Read by bash. These MUST be LF on disk everywhere -- including a Windows
# checkout that a student then runs inside WSL or Git Bash.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf

# Current GNU make and BuildKit both tolerate CRLF, so these are defensive
# rather than urgent: macOS ships an older make, and the first `RUN ./x.sh`
# added to a Dockerfile would make it urgent without warning.
Makefile      text eol=lf
*.mk          text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.dockerfile  text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts. PowerShell reads either, but CRLF keeps them correct
# in Notepad and in the Windows console.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf

# The .ipynb files are generated from the marimo .py next to them. Pinned to LF
# so the committed bytes are identical no matter who ran `make mirrors`, and
# collapsed in GitHub diffs to keep PR review readable.
#
# On a merge conflict in one of these, do NOT resolve it by hand:
#     git checkout --ours <file> && make mirrors
*.ipynb  text eol=lf linguist-generated=true

# Never translate these.
*.mp4   binary
*.onnx  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
